      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f2fe2a7d-ded8-535a-87fb-25d653347bf2",
      ":question/problem": "The growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between its maximum capacity and its current population. Let $N(t)$ be the number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum capacity is $20$ deer, which differential equation models this population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "74dc95f0-7a26-55c5-abfd-cccf411a9901",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "66bdd2bf-99f3-59e1-ab7f-5117bf60546d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(57-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "93c6efab-1ed7-5593-963b-10b1cd27665f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(20-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8f4096b4-3e30-5b2a-a561-c373ecd7ec59",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(94-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c69aefcb-d8e7-57fd-9ccc-5b7ef20a0d61",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(28-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ae0c9cd2-ca87-5cff-a5cb-04d1eec7285a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(76-N)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "93c6efab-1ed7-5593-963b-10b1cd27665f"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current quantity. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=20$, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(20-N).\n$$"
    },
